  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nThe dry air punch was nice this morning, but it's short-lived. \n70F+ dews just to our south overspreading the region now will \nsoon complete the transaction. Thence, the heat comes in earnest,\nwith the entire area experiencing triple digit indices thru the\nmid week and headlined accordingly. Should Thursday be added as\nwell? It does not look like there is collaborative stomach for \nthat push today, but HI's are similar, if mostly just shy of the\nhard single day criteria. The NWS Heat Risk map reflects some \ncontraction Thursday that begins a trend that carries on \ninto/thru the weekend, even as we do have signals in the model \nguidance that we remain above normal...probably we fall off the \nmid week week extremes enough to preclude headlines\n(eventually--by the weekend) but we'll see as it plays out. \nAlready, today's guidance numbers are higher/pops are lower vs \nthe preceding day vs the preceding day, so we're trending \nwarmer/drier even with cooling; something to monitor. Probably \nthe height falls and reemerging pops by early next week pushes \nus out of the extremes. Until then, SEE the next 2-3 days of \nrecord or near record breaking temps:\n\nTUESDAY SEPTEMBER 15\nSTATION    FCST HI    RECORD HI/YR\nCGI\t\t\t96\t\t\t96/2025\nMDH \t\t96\t\t   106/1939\nEVV  \t\t98\t\t    99/1939\nPAH\t\t\t97\t\t   102/1939\nPOF\t\t\t98\t\t   101/1939\n\nWEDNESDAY SEPTEMBER 16\nSTATION    FCST HI    RECORD HI/YR\nCGI \t\t95\t\t    99/2019\nMDH \t\t96\t\t   101/1927 \nEVV \t\t97\t\t\t97/1897\nPAH\t\t\t97\t\t\t97/2019\nPOF\t\t\t98\t\t   101/1927\n\nTHURSDAY SEPTEMBER 17\nSTATION\t   FCST HI\t  RECORD HI/YR\nCGI \t\t96 \t\t    96/2019\nMDH\t\t\t96\t\t   102/1927\nEVV\t\t\t99\t\t\t96/1927\nPAH\t\t\t96\t\t\t98/1939\nPOF\t\t\t98\t\t   101/1927\n\nOne could make a duration argument for the Advisory to run thru\nFriday, as we maintain triple digit HI production thru then; \nthe upper ridge continues to run strong in the mid-upper 590s \nDM (H5) thru the week's end. But after that, it is muddied up \nenough by low pressure areas barrelling into it over the weekend\nfrom both the north/west and south/east to drop her into the \n580s by early next week. Temps should cool off their peaks \n(while remaining above normal) while smallish pcpn chances \nreemerge in the forecast with this synoptic pattern evolution.",
